<PUNCTUATION>==</PUNCTUATION> <HEADING>Introduction</HEADING>

This document demonstrates <CONSTANT>*AsciiDoc*</CONSTANT> syntax for highlighting.
AsciiDoc is a lightweight markup language for writing documentation.

<PUNCTUATION>===</PUNCTUATION> <HEADING>Basic Formatting</HEADING>

Text can be <CONSTANT>*bold*</CONSTANT>, <STRING>_italic_</STRING>, <FUNCTION>`monospaced`</FUNCTION>, or [.underline]#underlined#.
You can also use <CONSTANT>**bold within**</CONSTANT> a word and <STRING>__italic within__</STRING> a word.

Superscript: E=mc^2^ and subscript: H~2~O.

<PUNCTUATION>===</PUNCTUATION> <HEADING>Links and Cross-References</HEADING>

Visit https://asciidoctor.org for more info.
See <FUNCTION>link:</FUNCTION><TAG>api.html</TAG><PUNCTUATION>[</PUNCTUATION><STRING>API Documentation</STRING><PUNCTUATION>]</PUNCTUATION> for details.
Cross-reference: <TAG>&lt;&lt;_tables,Tables section&gt;&gt;</TAG>

<PUNCTUATION>==</PUNCTUATION> <HEADING>Lists</HEADING>

<PUNCTUATION>===</PUNCTUATION> <HEADING>Unordered</HEADING>

<KEYWORD>*</KEYWORD> First item
<KEYWORD>**</KEYWORD> Nested item
<KEYWORD>***</KEYWORD> Deeply nested
<KEYWORD>*</KEYWORD> Second item
<KEYWORD>*</KEYWORD> Third item

<PUNCTUATION>===</PUNCTUATION> <HEADING>Ordered</HEADING>

<KEYWORD>.</KEYWORD> Step one
<KEYWORD>.</KEYWORD> Step two
<KEYWORD>..</KEYWORD> Sub-step a
<KEYWORD>..</KEYWORD> Sub-step b
<KEYWORD>.</KEYWORD> Step three

<PUNCTUATION>===</PUNCTUATION> <HEADING>Description List</HEADING>

Term 1:: Definition of term 1.
Term 2:: Definition of term 2.

<PUNCTUATION>==</PUNCTUATION> <HEADING>Code Blocks</HEADING>

Inline code: <FUNCTION>`System.out.println("Hello")`</FUNCTION>

<PUNCTUATION>.</PUNCTUATION><HEADING>A Java example</HEADING>
<PUNCTUATION>[</PUNCTUATION><ATTRIBUTE>source,java</ATTRIBUTE><PUNCTUATION>]</PUNCTUATION>
<PUNCTUATION>----</PUNCTUATION>
<FUNCTION>public class Hello {</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>    public static void main(String[] args) {</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>        System.out.println("Hello, World!");</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>    }</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>}</FUNCTION>
<PUNCTUATION>----</PUNCTUATION>

<PUNCTUATION>.</PUNCTUATION><HEADING>Shell commands</HEADING>
<PUNCTUATION>[</PUNCTUATION><ATTRIBUTE>source,bash</ATTRIBUTE><PUNCTUATION>]</PUNCTUATION>
